statement:
For every nonempty class $C$, $\sigma(C)=\max_R\min_{A\in\partial^+R}
u_k(A)$, where the maximum ranges over $R\subseteq2^C$ with $\emptyset\in R$ and $C
otin R$, and $\partial^+R=\{A\cup\{c\}:A\in R,\ c\in C\setminus A,\ A\cup\{c\}
otin R\}$. In particular, $\sigma(C)\geq t$ follows if every boundary class has an $r$-face with nonzero $\widetilde H_{i-1}(\mathcal B(A,F);k)$ and $r>it$.
